Comments:
1. Evaluator: Kiana Setoodehnia, August 14, 2024
2. The bound states' energies and spin-parities are from the 18Ne 2024-ENSDF evaluation by Kiana Setoodehnia.
3. The spectroscopic factors come from either T. K. Li et al., Phys. Rev. C 13 (1976) 55: 17O(d,p)18O, or from S. A. Kuvin et al., Phys. Rev. C 96 (2017) 045812:
   d(17F,n).
4. The resonance energies and spin-parities are also from the 18Ne 2024-ENSDF evaluation by Kiana Setoodehnia.
5. For the measured proton widths, see D. W. Bardayan et al., Phys. Rev. C, 62 (2000) 055804; Y. Parpottas et al., Phys. Rev. C 72 (2005) 025802; K. A. Chipps
   et al., Phys. Rev. Lett., 102 (2009) 152502; also see the 18Ne 2024-ENSDF evaluation by Kiana Setoodehnia.
6. For gamma-ray partial widths, see https://nucldata.tunl.duke.edu/nucldata/HTML/IntroTables/Table3_1995.pdf.
7. For the upper limit proton width, see S. H. Park et al., Phys. Rev. C59 (1999) 1182; and R. J. Charity et al., Phys. Rev. C 99 (2019) 044304.
8. The experimental rate is larger than the TALYS rate at 10 GK. Therefore, no high-temperature rate matching is needed.
